<title>USA: PP&amp;L faces scattered outages after winds.</title>
<headline>PP&amp;L faces scattered outages after winds.</headline>
<dateline>ALLENTOWN, Pa. 1997-03-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>PP&amp;L Resources Inc said on Thursday that high winds in eastern and central Pennsylvania have resulted in scattered power outages.</p>
<p>As of 1000 EST, about 13,000 Pennsyvania Power &amp; Light Co customers were without power, the company said.</p>
<p>Most of the problems were in the eastern portions of the company's service area, including the Lehigh Valley and Pike and Wayne counties in northeastern Pennsylvania, PP&amp;L said.  </p>
<p>PP&amp;L said crews have restored power to about 6,000 customers since the 50 mile-per-hour winds started last night.</p>
<p>PP&amp;L serves 1.2 million homes and businesses in eastern and central Pennsylvania.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk +1 212 859 1710))</p>
